ooRexx (third_party/ooRexx, a pinned unmodified submodule) is not part of this
repository's source, and built binaries contain none of its code. Its
interpreter is the reference the tests compare against. interrexx-classes and
interrexx-inventory generate tables of interface facts (class and method
names, arities, error numbers and error message texts) from Setup.cpp,
BuiltinFunctions.cpp and rexxmsg.xml at build time.

Attribution: the error message texts, and the error numbers and names they
belong to, come from the message catalogue of Open Object Rexx (ooRexx),
https://www.oorexx.org/, copyright the Rexx Language Association and its
contributors. ooRexx is distributed under the Common Public License 1.0,
https://opensource.org/license/cpl1-0-txt/.

ooTest and the ooRexx documentation are fetched by scripts/setup-third-party.sh
and are not redistributed here.
